---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const updated = "October 28, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — GoodFat"
  description="Terms for using GoodFat, including our experimental inflammatory score disclaimer."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 pb-24 pt-28 sm:px-8">
    <p class="label-micro text-yellow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-800 tracking-tight text-text">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      These terms are an agreement between you and GoodFat for use of the GoodFat app and website. By
      using GoodFat, you agree to them.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">1. What GoodFat is</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat helps you notice fat quality and inflammatory load in meals you log — through scans,
          barcodes, and chat. It is a personal education and awareness tool.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-panel border border-yellow/40 bg-card/60 p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">2. Inflammatory score — read this</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat’s inflammatory score is{" "}
          <strong class="text-text">educational and entirely experimental</strong>.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            It is <strong class="text-text">inspired by real nutrition research</strong> on fats,
            processing, and inflammation markers.
          </li>
          <li>
            It is <strong class="text-text">not a validated clinical score</strong>, medical device,
            diagnosis, or treatment.
          </li>
          <li>
            It has <strong class="text-text">not been proven</strong> in peer-reviewed trials as a
            measure of your personal health risk.
          </li>
          <li>
            Green / amber / red bands and number changes are for awareness and habit support only.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Do not use the score to change medicines, diagnose disease, or replace advice from a
          licensed clinician. If you have a health condition, talk to a professional you trust.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">3. Not medical advice</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Nothing in GoodFat — including chat replies, “better option” suggestions, omega estimates,
          NOVA labels, or scores — is medical, dietary, or clinical advice. Food swaps are ideas, not
          prescriptions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">4. Your account and responsibilities</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>You must be old enough to use the app where you live (at least 13 in the U.S.).</li>
          <li>You are responsible for what you log and for decisions you make from the app.</li>
          <li>
            You agree not to misuse the service (for example, trying to break security or harm others).
          </li>
          <li>
            Anonymous sessions may be created so chat and logging can work without an email. You can
            delete your account in Settings.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">5. Photos and scanning</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You may take or upload food photos and scan barcodes. You confirm you have the right to use
          those images. GoodFat uses Apple Intelligence and Vision on the iPhone to help identify food
          and <strong class="text-text">does not upload or save them as a photo library</strong>. See
          our{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">6. Data sources and estimates</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Nutrition and score estimates may come from:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Our on-device US food pack (drawing on public sources such as USDA and Open Food Facts)</li>
          <li>Your confirmed grams and entries</li>
          <li>
            Apple Intelligence on your iPhone, which names a food or answers a question. It does not
            supply nutrition numbers, and GoodFat does not invent missing fatty acids
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Catalogs and AI can be wrong or incomplete. Always use judgment with packaged labels and
          your own knowledge of what you ate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">7. Subscriptions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Some features may require a paid subscription. GoodFat 2.0 runs on iPhone. Purchases go
          through the Apple App Store via <strong class="text-text">RevenueCat</strong>. The checkout
          screen is GoodFat’s own paywall.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Prices and terms are shown before you buy.</li>
          <li>Renewals and cancellations follow App Store rules.</li>
          <li>Refunds are handled by Apple under its policies.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">8. Acceptable use of AI features</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Ask is for food and fat-quality questions related to your logging. It uses Apple Intelligence
          on your iPhone. Do not use it for emergencies, self-harm, or medical diagnosis. Replies can
          be wrong.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">9. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat’s name, logo, app design, and original content belong to us or our licensors. Public
          food databases remain subject to their own licenses and attribution rules. You keep rights
          to content you create (such as your log entries), and you grant us a limited license to
          process that content to run the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">10. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat is provided <strong class="text-text">“as is”</strong> and{" "}
          <strong class="text-text">“as available.”</strong> We do not warrant that scores, food IDs,
          or suggestions will be accurate, complete, or fit for a particular purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To the fullest extent allowed by law, GoodFat and its operators are not liable for
          indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss related
          to reliance on the inflammatory score, chat advice, or nutrition estimates. Our total
          liability for any claim about the service is limited to the greater of (a) amounts you paid
          us for the app in the 12 months before the claim, or (b) USD $50.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">Some places do not allow these limits; in those places, limits apply only as allowed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">12. Ending use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You may stop using GoodFat anytime and delete your account in Settings. We may suspend or
          stop the service or your access if you break these terms or if we shut the product down.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">13. Website use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The marketing site at goodfatbadfat.com is part of the GoodFat service. Optional website
          analytics run only after you accept them. See our{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="/privacy#cookies">
            Privacy policy
          </a>{" "}
          for cookies and local storage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">14. Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update these terms. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Continued use
          after updates means you accept the new terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">15. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Email{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="mailto:help@goodfatbadfat.com"
            >help@goodfatbadfat.com</a
          >. Privacy details are in our{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
